[{:db/id "q-24378/selection/3901d85cba21c4425bb1d00247eee1bafade7c5d71da9fefe236fd351b1e7c2d" :answer/id #uuid "f5ab26b6-08da-5425-8654-994a301549cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3(1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24378/selection/9de178e4740b419a248f664b416763c024115124bb4c77ebca7a599f853094e0" :answer/id #uuid "85c9a6ce-7931-5053-8f42-5a2270259829" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24378/selection/7cd50060b597262128d08342b8745ad470dd06b4a320c43aa3aa29a86a11353b" :answer/id #uuid "dc5f842c-bee5-53ec-b816-9d6d014e513f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24378/selection/f52329ed476e687f486aafacbb7973cf97cce59b5c01a463b45d3ea4120d7cec" :answer/id #uuid "876b5dc7-1fb2-5f36-929d-970b1e677209" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3(1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24378/selection/090e737a87285d3b906cc9010647fae8a2cc9ab0cfcedc54e61d78183a37b95b" :answer/id #uuid "19c9a8c6-e009-53b4-b12c-0191de7a91a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2(1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24378/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a92445cb-46d5-5049-82b6-6f64444df8e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-24378/selection/f52329ed476e687f486aafacbb7973cf97cce59b5c01a463b45d3ea4120d7cec" :answer-field/choices ["q-24378/selection/3901d85cba21c4425bb1d00247eee1bafade7c5d71da9fefe236fd351b1e7c2d" "q-24378/selection/9de178e4740b419a248f664b416763c024115124bb4c77ebca7a599f853094e0" "q-24378/selection/7cd50060b597262128d08342b8745ad470dd06b4a320c43aa3aa29a86a11353b" "q-24378/selection/f52329ed476e687f486aafacbb7973cf97cce59b5c01a463b45d3ea4120d7cec" "q-24378/selection/090e737a87285d3b906cc9010647fae8a2cc9ab0cfcedc54e61d78183a37b95b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-24378" :question/id #uuid "615bfb39-f4dc-5e2d-9395-b7631c9499f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-24378" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using double angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =(1-{sin}^{2}⁡t)-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=\\frac{x}{2}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{3}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{3} & =1-2{(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =1-2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2} \\\\ y & =3(1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=3(1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-24378/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "78dbecb4-68d4-53b0-b47f-f37ce92da896"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-24378"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102668/selection/621e351bd2aa0a6fcb7d8e3f2570df97b7c36e0bd976170a2375ff8bfa554262" :answer/id #uuid "da9cd34f-c2ab-518b-8132-46abdb181301" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2(2x+1)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102668/selection/63c519a2bf4c18ca9b342715ffeb76449f58eb485129c2fb434cf584c57e2507" :answer/id #uuid "a2e14081-8b1c-529e-ae73-129b8cac5b07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4x(x+5)(2x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102668/selection/4a8d4b6af5eacd08171c3320a22d5d679a7b8a7190497feb579487f9be7a0eb2" :answer/id #uuid "b65139e2-0c50-5423-b3a0-6c9691d0733a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4x(2x+1)(2x-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102668/selection/1762e2ee690f75ae45db57180301705146ec5da2156f83c6065ef191b79bd41f" :answer/id #uuid "158970c7-5b1d-57f4-9b6a-03b6ca1ae2cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x(x-5)(2x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102668/selection/0860209cab1584dd19ee00be7d98cc074c05ab9705a55f5c6eaedfbe9c97f2f6" :answer/id #uuid "ab374465-0f5d-5ef1-ac40-b3e35c2ef8a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=(2x+1)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102668/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e83a50a6-01bf-5730-9930-1af38c0fb461" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102668/selection/63c519a2bf4c18ca9b342715ffeb76449f58eb485129c2fb434cf584c57e2507" :answer-field/choices ["q-102668/selection/621e351bd2aa0a6fcb7d8e3f2570df97b7c36e0bd976170a2375ff8bfa554262" "q-102668/selection/63c519a2bf4c18ca9b342715ffeb76449f58eb485129c2fb434cf584c57e2507" "q-102668/selection/4a8d4b6af5eacd08171c3320a22d5d679a7b8a7190497feb579487f9be7a0eb2" "q-102668/selection/1762e2ee690f75ae45db57180301705146ec5da2156f83c6065ef191b79bd41f" "q-102668/selection/0860209cab1584dd19ee00be7d98cc074c05ab9705a55f5c6eaedfbe9c97f2f6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102668" :question/id #uuid "f662300f-f189-53c3-b854-815e04ddab5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-102668" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{t-5}{2},\\,\\,\\,y=({t}^{2}-25)(t-4),\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{t-5}{2}\\,⇒\\,t=2x+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=2x+5$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =((2x+5)^{2}-25)(2x+5-4) \\\\  & =(4{x}^{2}+20x+25-25)(2x+1) \\\\  & =(4{x}^{2}+20x)(2x+1) \\\\  & =4x(x+5)(2x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=4x(x+5)(2x+1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-102668/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79107609-77e6-55e9-970d-da63c39daf0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102668"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321084/field-1/0fbba6d952c8d264be70d774d4feef7f24de7b82196534babc5d3bd99d66497c" :answer/id #uuid "0b02216e-1888-53d2-a339-64d43470e022" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x^4+6x^2-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321084/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "efc94e2d-73ec-5487-af0a-0d200a851b62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321084/field-1/0fbba6d952c8d264be70d774d4feef7f24de7b82196534babc5d3bd99d66497c" :answer-field/choices ["q-321084/field-1/0fbba6d952c8d264be70d774d4feef7f24de7b82196534babc5d3bd99d66497c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321084" :question/id #uuid "9c4b3f61-cafc-57f5-8068-37339299eacb" :question/math-academy-id "q-321084" :question/problem "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{\\,t+1\\,},\\,\\,\\,y=t(4-t),\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\sqrt{\\,t+1\\,}\\,⇒\\,t={x}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t={x}^{2}-1$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =({x}^{2}-1)(4-({x}^{2}-1)) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-1)(5-{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=({x}^{2}-1)(5-{x}^{2}).$\n\nFinally, since $t\\ge 0$ and $t={x}^{2}-1,$ we must have ${x}^{2}-1\\ge 0,$ i.e., $x\\ge 1.$\n\nTherefore, the complete Cartesian equation is $y=({x}^{2}-1)(5-{x}^{2}),\\,x\\ge 1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321084/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79107609-77e6-55e9-970d-da63c39daf0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321084"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
